## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design privacy-conscious, region-aware ML in production with strict latency and governance guarantees. Requires balancing privacy (DP/FL) with performance, cross-region drift, and auditable retraining.

## Key Concepts
- Federated learning
- Differential privacy
- Feature hashing
- Drift detection
- Calibration
- Retraining cadence
- Latency constraints

## Code Example
```javascript
function hashFeatureKeys(keys) {
  // simple 1024-bin hash
  const bins = new Array(1024).fill(0);
  for (const k of Object.keys(keys)) {
    const hash = [...k].reduce((a,c)=> (a*31+c.charCodeAt(0))>>>0, 7);
    bins[hash % 1024] += keys[k];
  }
  return bins;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor privacy leakage risk in FL setting?
- How would you validate calibration across regions with limited labeled data?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical baseline ML for streaming signals with delayed labels, focusing on CPU constraints and simple online learning.

## Key Concepts
- Online updates with partial_fit
- Drift detection (PSI/KS)
- Calibration (Platt scaling)
- Simple retraining cadence and data splits

## Code Example
